#!/usr/bin/env python3
import json, sys
OUT=sys.argv[1]; s=json.load(open(OUT+'/SUMMARY.json')); L=[]; A=L.append
mb=lambda b: f"{b/1e6:.1f} MB"
A('# Drive byte-identity crosswalk, 24 October 2026\n')
A('Data only. Scientific effect NONE. Credit 0. Not a review, a binding or a status change: Drive sources stay UNBOUND (GB-5). It joins the existing 2026-09-17 Drive catalog to Git, to the Dropbox `Github/` hashes of `audits/dropbox_import/2026-10-24` (main#594) and to two reassembled archives; it creates no second catalog.\n')
A('## Inputs\n')
A(f"- **Drive side.** {s['snapshot']}: {s['items']['snapshot_items']:,} items plus {s['items']['delta_items']} delta items (one record per Drive id; an id listed in a delta and in the inventory, or in two deltas, is counted once); {s['items']['files_non_personal']:,} files outside the personal lane ({s['items']['files_personal_lane_counted_only']} files in `03_PERSONAL_AND_EARLIER_RESEARCH` are counted and not listed). {s['hashed_files']['count_including_personal_lane']:,} files carry a SHA-256 in that publication (binary originals and stored delta objects), {s['hashed_files']['count']:,} of them outside the personal lane; native Google Docs carry none.")
A("- **Rule.** For a non-empty file of 4 MiB or less the Dropbox `content_hash` is the SHA-256 of its SHA-256 (an empty file's is the SHA-256 of nothing) (the rule `tools/dropbox_reconcile.py` implements), so the published digests are matched to the Dropbox table without any download. Git blobs and archive members are matched by SHA-256 directly, so the 4 MiB limit affects only the Dropbox column (" + str(s['hashed_files']['over_4mib_dropbox_not_derivable']) + " files).")
A("- **Git side.** Every blob reachable from the fetched refs of main (all remote branches, unshallowed) and Math- (main and PR refs): 32,221 blobs, the same index as main#594. `git_where` says whether a matching blob is on a tip as of the index tips listed in `PINS.json` (`TIP`), found in Git only under `drive/` paths (`DRIVE_MIRROR_BRANCH`: the mirror tree, on main from 18 to 23 September 2026 and on the hardening branches; `f35eef1b` reverted it from main) or elsewhere in history (`BRANCH_OR_HISTORY`).")
A("- **Liveness.** A connector search for items with `modifiedTime` after 2026-09-17T00:00Z (ten windows, metadata only). That cutoff precedes the snapshot taken that day, so an item modified on 17 September is `MODIFIED_ON_SNAPSHOT_DAY` (digest `UNCERTAIN_SNAPSHOT_DAY`); an item whose `modifiedTime` equals its `createdTime` was never modified after creation (`SAME_AS_CREATED`, digest `CURRENT`); an item modified on 18 September or later is `MODIFIED_AFTER_SNAPSHOT_DAY`, and its snapshot digest is `CURRENT` only if a dated delta (18–20 September) re-hashed it at or after that modification, otherwise `STALE` or `STALE_SAME_SIZE` (same byte count; moves and renames bump the time; identity not re-verified). Items not in the search are `NOT_MODIFIED_SINCE_2026-09-17`. Items unknown to the snapshot are `NEW_SINCE_SNAPSHOT` and counted only.\n")
A('## Tiers (files outside the personal lane)\n')
A('| tier | files | files in published parts | bytes of published parts (rounded to 100 KB) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|')
for t,v in s['tiers'].items(): A(f"| `{t}` | {v['files']:,} | {v['files_in_published_parts']:,} | {mb(v['bytes_rounded_published_parts'])} |")
A('\nA tier byte total covers only the parts that print bytes elsewhere here (rows with public bytes, and aggregate cells of three files or more); files in count-only cells and title-public rows without public bytes are left out, so no withheld size can be recovered by differencing.')
gw=s['git_exact_where']; A(f"\n`GIT_EXACT` by location: {', '.join(f'{k} {v:,}' for k,v in sorted(gw.items()))}. `NO_DIGEST` are native Google Docs and a few delta rows without a stored object; `FOLDER` rows are not files.\n")
d=s['dropbox_overlap']; A(f"**Dropbox overlap.** {d['drive_files_byte_identical_to_a_dropbox_github_file']:,} Drive files are byte-identical to a Dropbox `Github/` file. Of the {d['dropbox_only_distinct_contents_total']} distinct contents that main#594 found only in Dropbox, {d['dropbox_only_distinct_contents_also_in_drive']} also exist in Drive at the snapshot.\n")
am=s['archive_members']; A(f"**Archive members.** The publication lists {am['total']:,} members of {am['carriers']} Drive archive carriers with payload digests: {am['preserved'].get('MEMBER',0):,} are themselves in Git, Dropbox or an archive, {am['preserved'].get('VIA_CARRIER',0):,} are preserved because their carrier is, and {am['preserved'].get('NOT_FOUND',0):,} are found in none of the three places ({', '.join(f'{v:,} inside {k} carriers' for k,v in sorted(am['not_found_by_carrier_tier'].items()))}; the over-4 MiB carriers' Dropbox identity is not derivable, nor is that of the {s['archive_members_not_found_over_4mib']} members themselves over 4 MiB). Carriers by tier: {', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k,v in sorted(am['carriers_by_tier'].items()))}.\n")
lv=s['liveness']; A(f"**Liveness.** The ten listing agents each reported their window complete ({lv['windows_complete']}; a self-report, see Limits); {lv['live_items_seen'] or 0:,} live items seen. Snapshot files by live status: {', '.join(f'{k} {v:,}' for k,v in sorted(lv['files_by_live_status'].items()))}. Hashed files by digest state: {', '.join(f'{k} {v:,}' for k,v in sorted(lv['hashed_files_by_digest_state'].items()))}. New since the snapshot: {lv['new_since_snapshot']['items']:,} items ({lv['new_since_snapshot']['folders']} folders), {lv['new_since_snapshot']['titles_in_drv_maps']} with a title already in the DRV maps, {lv['new_since_snapshot']['parent_not_in_snapshot']:,} under a parent the snapshot does not know; counted by class in `SUMMARY.json`, not listed.\n")
lg=s['ledger']; A(f"## Coverage ledger\n\nThe 344-row coverage ledger has {lg['missing_proof_rows']} units with a `MISSING` proof source; {lg['missing_proof_rows_without_dropbox_name_hit']} of them had no Dropbox name hit of either strength in main#594 (48 had one: 30 printed at row level there, 18 only in its aggregated `ledger_hits`). The same name rule applied to Drive paths below the hub gives {lg['name_hits']} hits over all 344 rows, {lg['missing_proof_rows_hit']} `MISSING`-proof rows among them, {len(lg['missing_proof_rows_hit_without_dropbox_name_hit'])} of those without a Dropbox name hit (rows {', '.join(map(str,lg['missing_proof_rows_hit_without_dropbox_name_hit']))}). None is `STRONG`; by class the hits are {', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k,v in sorted(lg['hits_by_match'].items()))}, and {lg['hits_by_where'].get('folder',0)} of them match only in a folder segment. Of the {len(lg['missing_proof_rows_hit_without_dropbox_name_hit'])} rows without a Dropbox name hit, {len(lg['rows_without_dropbox_name_hit_reached_only_by_lone_tokens'])} are reached only by one rare token in a prose title (`WEAK_LONE`, the weakest class: {lg['lone_token_hits_on_prose_titles_over_8_stem_tokens']} of the lone-token hits fall on titles of more than eight tokens); none is unit-specific. Of the {lg['missing_proof_hits']} hits on `MISSING`-proof rows, the items are {', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k,v in sorted(lg['hit_item_tiers'].items()))}. The rule is the main#594 rule byte for byte, applied to the path below the hub and its package folder (title only where a delta item has no path); it is name evidence only, labelled per hit in `LEDGER_DRIVE_ROWS.tsv` (`match`, `where`).\n")
dm=s['drv_maps']; A(f"## Join to the DRV maps\n\n{dm['snapshot_files_with_a_title_in_the_maps']} snapshot files carry a title that `docs/retro/DRV-H2/DRV-H2.map.csv` ({dm['drv_h2_rows']} rows) or `docs/retro/DRV-H3/DRV-H3_drive_map.csv` ({dm['drv_h3_rows']} rows) already prints; {s['drv_map_digests']['title_public_files_with_digest']} of them have a snapshot digest, printed for the {s['drv_map_digests']['of_which_digest_printed']} whose bytes are already public (`GIT_EXACT`, `ARCHIVE_EXACT`) and withheld for the rest ({', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k,v in sorted(s['drv_map_digests']['withheld_by_tier'].items()))}; held locally). The maps keep their objects; nothing here binds.\n")
A('## Files\n')
A(f"- `DRIVE_CROSSWALK.tsv`: {s['row_level_rows']:,} per-file rows under the row-level rule ({s['row_level_rule']}).")
A(f"- `DRIVE_AGGREGATE.tsv`: the {s['aggregate_files']:,} files that have no per-file row, by hub, tier and class (so no cell can be differenced against the per-file rows); cells below three files are merged into `(other)` per hub and tier, and a cell still below three prints its file count only. Delta manifest folders are one generic hub label.")
A(f"- `LEDGER_DRIVE.tsv`: one line per ledger unit with hits (counts by strength and tier); `LEDGER_DRIVE_ROWS.tsv`: per-item lines for public items only. `ARCHIVE_CARRIERS.tsv`: {s['carrier_rows']} per-carrier lines where the title is on main or the bytes are public, the other carriers aggregated by tier.")
A('- `SUMMARY.json`, `PINS.json` (input blobs and local files by hash), `own/` (the scripts, with local roots replaced).\n')
A('## Limits\n')
A('- Byte identity says a file is preserved somewhere; it says nothing about canonical copies, review status or correctness.')
A('- Digests come from the 2026-09-17 publication and the 18–20 September deltas; the connector exposes no checksum, so nothing modified after the last delta (2026-09-20) has a current digest here, and no file was downloaded.')
A('- The live listing is metadata from a modified-after search: it cannot show deletions or trashing (`NOT_MODIFIED_SINCE_2026-09-17` means not re-modified, not still present), its completeness is the listing agents\' self-report (one window returned no items), duplicate lines across page boundaries were de-duplicated by id, and items whose parent the snapshot does not know are counted without a hub.')
A('- Byte totals are rounded to 100 KB and tier totals cover published parts only, so a withheld file\'s size cannot be recovered by differencing; the RESULT post of 22:41Z quoted whole-tier totals (rounded), which are not combinable with this directory\'s cells for that purpose either, because the cells here exclude the files whose bytes those totals also covered only in aggregate.')
A('- Items created after the snapshot are counted, not identified; their names are not public and their parents are often folders the snapshot does not know.')
A('- Row-level hashes of non-public files and the id-level crosswalk are held locally by the author and offered to the owner or the CoS.')
open(OUT+'/README.md','w',encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(L)+'\n'); print('readme', len('\n'.join(L)),'bytes')
